      "text": [
        " لِحَافٍ وَ هُوَ صَائِمٌ قَالَ «يَجْعَلُ بَيْنَهُمَا ثَوْباً».\nوَ قَدْ رَوَى عَبْدُ اَللَّهِ بْنُ سِنَانٍ عَنْهُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : «رُخْصَةً لِلشَّيْخِ فِي اَلْمُبَاشَرَةِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1882 - Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated from Abu Ja'far (as) that he was asked about a man who feels cold. Can he share a blanket with his wife while fasting?\nImam (as) said: \"He should place a cloth between them.\"\nIt is narrated from Abdullah ibn Sinan, from Imam (as):\n\"[There is] a concession for the elderly in physical closeness.\"  - permitting physical closeness for an elderly person."
        ]
      }
